title: Hunger Strike
subtitle: A comrade refuses food in prison.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('c_hunger'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
var c = RG.lw.fire('c_hunger');
RG.lw.setC('cm', c);
Q.lw_n = RG.lw.rnd(9, 16);
RG.news(c.name + ' on hunger strike in prison', 2);
!}

= Hunger Strike

**[+ lw_cm_name +]** has eaten nothing for [+ lw_n +] days. The demand is simple: to be treated as a political prisoner, with books, letters and visits, and not as a common criminal sewing mailbags. Seven other political prisoners in the same jail have joined in.

The prison doctor has written to the governor that the force-feeding will begin on Monday. A message on cigarette paper, smuggled out with the laundry, asks the party not to let it end in silence.

- @campaign: Make the hunger strike known in every works.
- @stop: Ask [+ lw_cm_name +] to end it.
- @spread: Call on every political prisoner in Germany to join it.
- @minister: Ask the social democratic ministers to intervene.

@campaign
subtitle: The country hears of it. The prison may give way, and the party gains respect.
on-arrival: {!
Q.worker_support += 3;
if (Math.random() < 0.45) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    RG.free(Q.lw_cm, {news: Q.lw_cm_name + ' released after hunger strike', priority: 2});
} else {
    Q.lw_out = 2;
}
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 3);
!}

Meetings in every district, a poster with a photograph, a delegation of mothers to the Ministry of Justice. [? if lw_out = 1 : After three weeks, the ministry decides that [+ lw_cm_name +] is too ill to be held, and releases the prisoner to a sanatorium, from which the prisoner walks out a week later. ?][? if lw_out = 2 : The ministry gives way on books and letters. [+ lw_cm_name +] eats again, and stays inside. ?]

@stop
subtitle: The party does not want a martyr it did not choose. The comrade's current thinks it heartless.
on-arrival: {!
var c = RG.comrade(Q.lw_cm);
if (c) { RG.lw.lean(c.faction, 0, -4); }
Q.unity += 1;
!}

A letter from the Zentrale reaches the cell: the party needs [+ lw_cm_name +] alive and well when the doors open. The hunger strike ends. The other seven end theirs too, more slowly.

@spread
subtitle: Every political prisoner refuses food. A great stir, and great risk. The Left's answer.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.militancy += 3;
Q.repression += 2;
Q.worker_support += 2;
if (Math.random() < 0.3) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    RG.free(Q.lw_cm, {news: Q.lw_cm_name + ' freed as prisons give way', priority: 2});
} else {
    Q.lw_out = 2;
}
RG.news('Political prisoners on hunger strike across Germany', 2);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 2, 5);
!}

Within a week, four hundred prisoners are refusing food, in Moabit, in Lichtenau, in Straubing. The papers are full of it. [? if lw_out = 1 : The government decides that one release is cheaper than four hundred funerals, and [+ lw_cm_name +] is the one. ?][? if lw_out = 2 : The prisons hold out longer than the prisoners. One by one, they eat. ?]

@minister
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A quiet word through the social democrats. It may work; it will be remembered.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids asking favours of the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('united_front');
Q.spd_relation += 3;
if (Math.random() < 0.6) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    var c = RG.comrade(Q.lw_cm);
    if (c && c.until > 0) { c.until = Math.max(Q.time + 1, c.until - 4); }
}
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 1, 3);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 0, -2);
!}

A deputy of ours has a quiet drink with a social democrat on the justice committee, who knows the minister. [? if lw_out = 1 : [+ lw_cm_name +] is moved to fortress custody, with books and visitors, and the sentence is cut. ?][? if lw_out = 0 : The minister regrets that he cannot interfere with the courts. ?]
